---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout 
  title="High Energy Astrophysics Cheat Sheet | Free X-rays, Gamma Rays, Cosmic Rays"
  description="Complete high energy astrophysics cheat sheet with X-rays, gamma rays, and cosmic rays. Free download for physics students."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>High Energy Astrophysics<br><span>Cheat Sheet</span></h1>
    <p>X-rays, gamma rays, and cosmic rays. From particle acceleration to extreme environments.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>X-ray Astronomy</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>X-ray Sources</h3>
        <pre><code>X-ray binaries: accreting neutron star/black hole
Active galactic nuclei: supermassive black hole
Supernova remnants: shocked gas
Galaxy clusters: hot intracluster medium
Solar corona: million-degree plasma</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Processes</h3>
        <pre><code>Thermal emission: blackbody + bremsstrahlung
Non-thermal: synchrotron, inverse Compton
Absorption: photoelectric, Compton
Scattering: Thomson, Klein-Nishina</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Gamma-ray Astronomy</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Gamma-ray Sources</h3>
        <pre><code>Gamma-ray bursts: most luminous events
Pulsars: rotating neutron stars
AGN jets: relativistic beaming
Solar flares: magnetic reconnection
Cosmic ray interactions</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Cosmic Rays</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Properties</h3>
        <pre><code>Composition: 90% protons, 9% He, 1% heavier
Energy range: 10⁹ - 10²⁰ eV
Origin: Galactic (supernovae), extragalactic (AGN?)
Spectrum: power law with knee/ankle
GZK limit: > 5 × 10¹⁹ eV (CMB interaction)</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Particle Acceleration</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Mechanisms</h3>
        <pre><code>Fermi acceleration: shock waves
Synchrotron radiation: charged particles in B field
Bremsstrahlung: deceleration in electric field
Inverse Compton: photons gain energy from electrons
Pair production: γ → e⁺e⁻ (in strong B field)</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Download</h2>
    <p>Print this page or save as PDF for quick reference.</p>
    <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Use Ctrl+P (Cmd+P on Mac) to print or save as PDF.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
